      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right that without a secure border, the government loses control, and the chaos of unmanaged migration will inevitably overwhelm our social services and strain our economy. However, true stability isn't just about keeping people out; it's about managing the flow so that the country can function without constant emergency responses. If we only focus on enforcement without a pathway to citizenship, we create a permanent underclass that fuels resentment and instability, whereas a balanced approach that secures the border while offering a clear route to legal status is the only way to achieve genuine, lasting peace.",
